# Curated static-analysis set, not clang-tidy's full catalogue: a first pass
# against a mature codebase with everything on produces mostly undifferentiated
# noise. Four groups, chosen for what they catch that the compiler warnings in
# cmake/CompilerWarnings.cmake do not:
#   bugprone-*       - real defect patterns (use-after-move, dangling
#                      references, suspicious casts, off-by-one idioms)
#   clang-analyzer-* - the Clang Static Analyzer's path-sensitive engine
#                      (null dereference, leaks, dead stores reachable only on
#                      some paths)
#   performance-*    - avoidable copies/allocations in hot codec paths
#   cert-*           - a deliberately narrow CERT C++ subset (see the
#                      Checks list below); most of cert-* either duplicates a
#                      bugprone-* check under a different name or targets C
#                      idioms (atoi, strcpy) this C++23, no-C-string codebase
#                      does not use, so most of the group is excluded rather
#                      than fired and ignored.
#
# NOT enabled, on purpose:
#   modernize-*, readability-*, google-*, llvm-*, hicpp-*, fuchsia-*, etc. -
#   stylistic/opinionated groups that would relitigate this codebase's own
#   deliberate conventions (see src/forge/'s comment-voice and
#   abstraction-avoidance patterns) rather than find defects.
# Three checks excluded from their otherwise-enabled groups, each verified
# against this codebase's actual output rather than excluded a priori:
#
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters - 59 hits, all API-design advice
#     ("these two int parameters could be swapped by a caller"), not a defect
#     pattern - fixing it means reordering or wrapping parameters across the
#     codec's call graph, which is the "broad stylistic churn" this project's
#     conventions rule out for its own sake.
#
#   bugprone-misplaced-widening-cast, bugprone-implicit-widening-of-
#   multiplication-result - 27 + 7 hits, all `narrow-typed-value * small-
#   constant` widened to size_t/int for use as an array index or bit count
#   (spot-checked across core/mdct.cpp, core/exponents.cpp, decoder.cpp,
#   eac3_decoder.cpp, oba/oamd.cpp). Every operand traces back to either a
#   loop index bounded by a codec block/group dimension (<=1536) or a
#   spec-fixed bitstream field width (<=8 bits, so <=255) - the product
#   cannot approach int/size_t range in this codebase, unlike the general
#   case these checks exist for. ASan+UBSan's own integer-overflow-adjacent
#   checks (see cmake/Sanitizers.cmake) already cover the case where a value
#   escapes its assumed range, which is the more precise tool for exactly
#   this class of bug - see the coupling-exponent precedent in 8386c8f.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-misplaced-widening-cast,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  cert-dcl21-cpp,
  cert-dcl50-cpp,
  cert-dcl58-cpp,
  cert-env33-c,
  cert-err33-c,
  cert-err34-c,
  cert-err52-cpp,
  cert-err58-cpp,
  cert-err60-cpp,
  cert-flp30-c,
  cert-mem57-cpp,
  cert-msc50-cpp,
  cert-msc51-cpp,
  cert-oop54-cpp,
  cert-oop57-cpp,
  cert-oop58-cpp,
  cert-pos44-c,
  cert-pos47-c,
  cert-str34-c

WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '(src/(forge|matroska)|apps/cli)/.*'
FormatStyle: none
